{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 18, :comments ["<b>For</b>. When he sought to know wisdom, he saw that the sage who recognizes the affairs of the world — through his abundance of wisdom he will always have vexation and pain, and he will not rejoice in children, because of his knowledge that their end is death in his lifetime or after him; nor in wealth — it flies away like a bird and also will not avail or save on the day of calamity; and the day of death is set between his two eyes."], :book :ecclesiastes, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 1, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Wikisource" "https://he.wikisource.org/wiki/%D7%90%D7%91%D7%9F_%D7%A2%D7%96%D7%A8%D7%90_%D7%A2%D7%9C_%D7%A7%D7%94%D7%9C%D7%AA"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:27:06.466500629Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}